; Gross-comparison detector fixture (test/semantic/check_all.py --gross).
; The balance assignments telescope to the same net total either way,
; so the net comparison cannot see how the assignments resolve; the
; gross columns can.  The harness's planted defect drops the first
; assignment's '= ' (reading it as a plain $300 amount instead of
; adjusting to $300, then to $50): every net row stays equal and the
; debit column of Assets:Cash moves from $300 to $400, which the
; oracle's --gross lines show and the planted C++ side no longer
; matches.
2012-01-01 Opening
    Assets:Cash  $100
    Equity:Opening

2012-01-02 Adjust
    Assets:Cash  = $300
    Equity:Adjustments

2012-01-03 Adjust
    Assets:Cash  = $50
    Equity:Adjustments
